  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "What is the value of the following expression?\n\n\\[\\frac{2}{1 - \\frac{2}{3}}\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-3\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac43\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac23\\)",
    "D": "\\(2\\)",
    "E": "\\(6\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "First calculate the entire denominator:\n\\[\n1-\\frac23=\\frac33-\\frac23=\\frac13.\n\\]\nThis denominator is nonzero. Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{1-\\frac23}=2\\div\\frac13=2\\times3=6.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(6\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
